    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW27wdcZpy5tWFoUfsGvALeMr)_\n\nBefore: the bespoke modules `sp-trails`, `sp-vc-ai-workbench` and `sp-vulpea-hierarchy` were spread over `academic/`, `prog/` and `text/`, next to modules that only configure other people's packages.\n\nAfter: they live in a new `libraries/modules/custom/` directory for custom, bespoke functionality. The tangle paths of the workbench and hierarchy docs point there, and the module tree in `docs/main.org` has a `custom/` section that says what the directory is for.\n\nHow: the `.el` files are moved with `git mv` and unchanged. `init.el` loads modules by name and the whole `modules/` tree is on the `load-path`, so nothing else needs to change. `sp-org-issues` is not included: it is not on main yet (it is in draft #3), so it needs the same move there.\n\nThis PR is based on #7 (which is based on #6). Retarget it to `main` once those are merged.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_013V6WSXthgpc9jPWyZsevsf)_",
